# For the owner to apply (his ruling of 18 November 2026: option (a), expiry 14 December 2026). Not applied by the conductor:
# it excepts a finding in the scanner. The commands, from the main checkout, in this order:
#
#   git apply OspreyFlow_Build/process/lanes/v062/slice-line/diffs/trivyignore-picomatch.diff
#   git add OspreyFlow_Core/.trivyignore
#   git commit -m "chore(security): accept CVE-2026-112366 (picomatch 4.0.7, build and test tooling only) until 14 December 2026, the owner's word" -- OspreyFlow_Core/.trivyignore
#   git push origin main        # only after GitHub's run on main has finished: a push cancels the run in progress
#
# Checked by the conductor on 18 November 2026, before writing the entry (the two facts the owner asked to be confirmed):
#   1. picomatch is in no image we build: `npm ls picomatch --omit=dev` from OspreyFlow_Core is empty; the only images
#      with a Node stage are the workspace's and the harness's, and in both the Node stage is a builder stage whose
#      output (`dist`) alone is copied into the final nginx or python image (apps/workspace/Dockerfile, harness/Dockerfile).
#   2. nothing in the product passes a person's input to it as a pattern: no file under apps, packages, services, harness or
#      scripts imports picomatch, micromatch, tinyglobby or fast-glob, or uses import.meta.glob; no package.json lists any of
#      them. Its users are vite, vitest and tinyglobby/fdir (reached from json-schema-to-typescript), which read patterns
#      from developers' config files at build and test time.
# Would GitHub's scans flag it too? The image scans: no, for fact 1. The `trivy` job (ci.yml, scan-type fs, no
# --include-dev-deps) passed on the latest run: picomatch is a dev dependency in the lockfile and that job leaves
# dev dependencies out. Only `make trivy` (which passes --include-dev-deps) reports it, so only the Mac's gate. The entry
# below applies to both anyway, since both read OspreyFlow_Core/.trivyignore.
diff --git a/OspreyFlow_Core/.trivyignore b/OspreyFlow_Core/.trivyignore
--- a/OspreyFlow_Core/.trivyignore
+++ b/OspreyFlow_Core/.trivyignore
@@ -110,3 +110,10 @@
 # dnspython again (excessive memory and CPU use; fixed in 2.9.2, on the same newer-Python line as above):
 # found by v0.5.1's release scan on 14 November 2026 and accepted by the owner on the same ground.
 CVE-2026-128089 exp:2026-12-14
